{"clock":1,"nonce":"16f8f7aa48db3fe30ab5cdf11af42866","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1791026890,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/EPFL-ENAC/eesd-modern-masonry-walls-db","event":"issue:5689192648"},"data":{"body":"Field #11 **Void Ratio** is documented in `Fields.csv` as `[%]`, \"Percentage of voids\", but the values come in four forms:\n\n| Form | Specimens | Examples | References |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fraction 0–1 | 81 | `0.25`, `0.45`, `0.48` | Bosiljkov \u0026 Tomazevic, Salmanpour et al., Fehling et al., Morandi et al., Inzunza Araya et al. (2027), … |\n| Percent range, with `%` | 16 | `25-55%`, `43-47%` | Modena et al. (2005), Inzunza Araya et al. (2026) |\n| Text | 74 | `solid` | Bosiljkov et al., Fehling \u0026 Stürz, Magenes et al., … |\n| Empty | 27 | | Fehling et al. (2007), Ötes et al., … |\n\nThe site shows the values as they are, but they can't be sorted, filtered or plotted as one quantity. For example, `0.45` and `45` would look like different voids.\n\n**Questions for EESD:**\n\n1. Are the fractions percentages divided by 100 (`0.45` = 45 %)?\n2. Should `solid` become `0` (and stay distinguishable from \"not reported\")?\n3. Should ranges stay as text (`25–55`), or be split into a min and a max, or a mean?\n\nOnce agreed, the fix belongs in the source xlsx/CSV. The converter then keeps the field numeric.\n\nRaised in #15.\n","title":"Void Ratio mixes fractions, percent ranges and text"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1791026890,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/EPFL-ENAC/eesd-modern-masonry-walls-db","event":"issue:5689192648"},"data":{"add":["task"],"remove":null}}]}